Windows fix: rules_pkg pkg_zip PackageZip action needs Python DLL dir on PATH.

rules_pkg 1.2.0's pkg_zip_impl invokes the build_zip py_binary with
use_default_shell_env=True plus a small hardcoded env dict:

    env = {"LANG": ..., "LC_CTYPE": ..., "PYTHONIOENCODING": ..., "PYTHONUTF8": ...}
    use_default_shell_env = True

On Windows this results in an action PATH curated by Bazel that omits
the Python toolchain's directory (where python313.dll lives). The
rules_python 2.x py_binary launcher.exe LoadLibrary's python313.dll at
process start and exits with STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND (0xC0000135) before
main() runs. Symptom: `PackageZip dist-test-stripped.zip failed:
(Exit -1073741515)` when Bazel packages an archive on Windows CI.

Fix: inject env["PATH"] = ctx.toolchains["@rules_python//python:toolchain_type"]
    .py3_runtime.interpreter.dirname on Windows. Overrides the shell PATH
Bazel would otherwise provide; no-op on Linux/macOS
(interpreter.basename doesn't end in .exe).

Applied via `single_version_override(patches=...)` on rules_pkg in
//MODULE.bazel. Candidate for upstreaming to bazelbuild/rules_pkg.

--- a/pkg/private/zip/zip.bzl	2026-07-14 23:02:54
+++ b/pkg/private/zip/zip.bzl	2026-07-14 23:06:33
@@ -65,18 +65,32 @@
 
     all_inputs = depset(direct = inputs, transitive = mapping_context.file_deps)
 
+    _env = {
+        "LANG": "en_US.UTF-8",
+        "LC_CTYPE": "UTF-8",
+        "PYTHONIOENCODING": "UTF-8",
+        "PYTHONUTF8": "1",
+    }
+
+    # Windows fix: rules_python 2.x py_binary launcher.exe LoadLibrary's
+    # python313.dll at process start. use_default_shell_env below gives the
+    # action a Bazel-curated PATH that doesn't include the Python toolchain
+    # directory (where python313.dll lives, co-located with python.exe in
+    # python-build-standalone). Override PATH here so the launcher finds
+    # the DLL. No-op on Linux/macOS.
+    _py = ctx.toolchains["@rules_python//python:toolchain_type"]
+    if _py and _py.py3_runtime and _py.py3_runtime.interpreter:
+        _interp = _py.py3_runtime.interpreter
+        if _interp.basename.endswith(".exe"):
+            _env["PATH"] = _interp.dirname
+
     ctx.actions.run(
         mnemonic = "PackageZip",
         inputs = all_inputs,
         executable = ctx.executable._build_zip,
         arguments = [args],
         outputs = [output_file],
-        env = {
-            "LANG": "en_US.UTF-8",
-            "LC_CTYPE": "UTF-8",
-            "PYTHONIOENCODING": "UTF-8",
-            "PYTHONUTF8": "1",
-        },
+        env = _env,
         use_default_shell_env = True,
     )
     return [
@@ -88,6 +102,7 @@
 
 pkg_zip_impl = rule(
     implementation = _pkg_zip_impl,
+    toolchains = ["@rules_python//python:toolchain_type"],
     # @unsorted-dict-items
